{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>He journeyed to Succot.</b> That is, the reason for the place being called <b>Succot</b> is that for his livestock he made booths (succot); therefore, etc. And it does not say ״to Succot״ — for then you would understand that before Jacob arrived it had already been called Succot, but that is not so. And if you say: is it really the case that just because Jacob made a booth there the place would be so called? Perhaps it is because he did an unprecedented thing, in his tender care for the livestock — something no person had done before, to prepare a booth for animals — and for this novel change he named the place accordingly."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:46.776676830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}